{"page_id": "olmo_long_tiny_text-11_pg161_pg1-p1", "markdown": "# PLU\n\nPLOWEFERE.\n\nCompanion in play. (4.-S.)\n\nPLOWKKY. Covered with pimples.\n\nFor hyme that is smetyne with his awenne blode, and spreds over alle his lymmes, and waxes plotokky, and brekes owtc.\n\nMS. Lincoln Med. f. 294.\n\nPLOW-LODE.\n\n\" Caracuta, plow lode,\" No-\n\nminale MS.\n\nIt seems to be the same as\n\nPlough-land, q. V.\n\n- A pump; a draw-well. Cornw.\n- A hard blow, Far. dial.\n- Directly; exactly.\n\nPLOWMELL.\n\nA small wooden hammer occa-\n\nsionally fixed to the plough, still used in the North; in the Midland counties in its stead is used a plough-hatchet.\n\nWeeping.\n\nPLOWRING., ploughshare. Kennett.\n\nPrompt. Paro.\n\nPLOWSHO.\n\nPLOY.\n\nA merry-meeting.\n\nNorth.\n\nPLOYE.\n\nPLUCK. (1) Courage.\n\nA plough. Nominale MSỊiẠạo pluck\n\nVar. dial.\n\nup one's heart,\" to be bold, to rejoice. Against the pluck, i. e. against the inclination.\n\n- To pluck a crow or goose with any one, i. e. to quarrel with him.\n- To pluck a rose, i. e. to go to the jakes, said of women. Middleton, iv. 222.\n- A dry pluck, i. e. a severe stroke. This same is kind cuckolds luck:\n\nThese fellowes have given ine a drie pluck, Now I have never a crose to blesse me.\n\nMariageof Witt and Wisdome, 1579.\n\n(5)\n\nOur kynge and Robyn rode togyder,\n\nForsoth as I you say, And they shote plucke buffet,\n\nAs they went by the way. Robin Hood, i. 75.\n\n(6) Same as (1) ?\n\n- I had the luck\n\nTo see, and drink a little pluck.\n\nBrome's Songs, 1661, p. 167.\n\n(7) A student who fails in an university examination is said to be plucked.\n\nPLUCKING.\n\nThe worsted plucked from the\n\nmachine while the wheel is turning. North.\n\nPLUERE.\n\nPLUF.\n\nWeeping. (4.-N.)\n\nA tube of tin through which boys blow\n\npeas. Linc.\n\nAlso called a pluffer.\n\nPLUFE.\n\nA plough.\n\nYorksh.\n\nPLUFFY. Spongy; porous. Deron. It is sometimes explained, soft, plump.\n\nPLUG.\n\nA dwarfish fellow. East.\n\nPLUM. (1) Light; soft.\n\nWest.\n\n- Sensible; honest. North.\n- Very; exceedingly.\n\n(4) Straight; upright; perpendicular.\n\nPlum\n\ndowne, Cotgrave in v. Escarpé.\n\n5) Plum round, quite round.\n\n\" Make their\n\nattire to sit plum roundạ Harrison, p. 172\n\nPlum fat, Florio, p. 33.\n\nPLUMAKIN.\n\nThe magnum-bonum plum.\n\nPLUME.\n\nTo pick or pluck the feathers off a\n\nhawk or other bird.\n\nPLUMED-SWAN.\n\nA white colour. One of the\n\nterms of ancient alchemy.\n\nPLUMMY.\n\nSoft; wet; mouldy. Devon.\n\nPLUMP. (1) Dry; hard.\n\nKent.\n\n- A clump of trees. North.\n- A crowd of people; a mass of anything.\n\nIt\n\nis sometimes a verb,\n\nto colleot together.\n\n633\n\nPOC\n\n\"Assemble theymselfes in plumpes,\" More's Supplycacyon of Soulys, sig. F. ii.\n\nRydes into rowte his dede to revenge, Presede into the plumpe and with a prynce metes,\n\nMorte Arthure, MS. Lincoln, f.76.\n\nWhen kynge Richard perceved that the people by\n\nplumpes fled from hym to Duke Henry.\n\nHall's Union, 1548.\n\nVar. dial. Forby has\n\nplumpendicular, perpendicular.\n\nPLUM-PORRIDGE.\n\nPorridge with plums in\n\nit, a favourite dish at Christmas in some parts of the country.\n\nIt is mentioned as part of\n\nChristmas fare in the Humourist, ed. 1724,\n\np. 22, and by Addison.\n\nPLUMP-PATE.\n\nPLUMPY.\n\nA thiek-headed fellow.\n\nTo churn. Corne.\n\nPLUMTEN.\n\nPlunged. Weber.\n\nPLUM-TREE.\n\nThe female pudendum.\n\nHave\n\nat the plum tree seems to have been either the burden of a song or a proverbial phrase.\n\nIt\n\noccurs in Middleton, although Mr. Dyce does not seem to be acquainted with the meaning of the term itself, which may be gathered from Cotgrave, in v. Hoche-prunier, and the Mariage of Witt and Wisdome, p. 16.\n\nPLUNGE. (1) A deep pool. Somerset\n\n(2) A strait or difficulty. Greene.\n\nPLUNGY.\n\nWet; rainy. (4.-N.)\n\nPLUNKET. A coarse woollen cloth PLUNKY.\n\nShort; thick; heavy East.\n\nPLUNT. A walking-stick, generally one which has a large knob.\n\nGlouc.\n\nPLURISY.\n\nSuperabundance.\n\nShak.\n\nPLUSHES. The thin hoops which hold a besom together.\n\nWest.\n\nPLY.\n\nTo bend; to consent, or comply. Still\n\nin use in Dorset, Barnes's Gl.\n\nPLYER.\n\nA very common bawd.\n\nPLYMOUTH-CLOAK.\n\nA cane, or stick.\n\nSo\n\ncalled, says Ray, ạẠạbecause we use a staff in cuerpo, but not when we wear a cloak.\"\n\nPO.\n\nA peacock.\n\n（4.-S.）\n\nA pruest proud ase a po, Seththe weddeth us bo.\n\nWright's Political Songs, p. 159.\n\nPOACHED. Land is said to be poached when it is trodden with holes by heavy cattle. Var.dia.\n\nPOACHING.\n\nSwampy\n\nDevon.\n\nPOAD-MILK. The first milk given by cow: after calving.\n\nSussex.\n\nPOARE-BLIND.\n\nDim-sighted.\n\nThe word\n\noccurs in Hollyband's Dictionarie, 1593.\n\nРОЛТ.\n\nTo kick.\n\nDevon.\n\nPOBS.\n\nPorridge.\n\nCraven.\n\nPOCHE.\n\nA pocket.\n\n（4.-N.）\n\nUnto another she dyde as moche ;\n\nFor they love none but for theyr poche.\n\nThe Complaynte of them that ben to late Maryed.\n\nPOCHEE.\n\nA dish in ancient cookery consisting\n\nprincipally of poached eggs. Pegge.\n\nPotters?\n\nPOCHIN.\n\nPOCHERS. A hedgehog. Somerset.\n\nPOCHIT. A pollard tree. Line.", "width": 987, "height": 1612, "blocks": [{"kind": "heading", "text": "PLU", "bbox": {"x": 258.50000025178576, "y": 67.1666663728125, "width": 53.71428571428572, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLOWEFERE.", "bbox": {"x": 73.85714269887754, "y": 110.82499997121423, "width": 144.35714285714286, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Companion in play. (4.-S.)", "bbox": {"x": 228.2857141738095, "y": 110.82499998134256, "width": 261.85714285714295, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLOWKKY. Covered with pimples.", "bbox": {"x": 77.21428554469807, "y": 134.33333332121566, "width": 329, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "For hyme that is smetyne with his awenne blode, and spreds over alle his lymmes, and waxes plotokky, and brekes owtc.", "bbox": {"x": 94.00000111505103, "y": 151.12499994512717, "width": 409.5714285714286, "height": 60.44999999999997}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "MS. Lincoln Med. f. 294.", "bbox": {"x": 318.92857126071425, "y": 191.42499998415886, "width": 184.64285714285714, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLOW-LODE.", "bbox": {"x": 73.8571426720696, "y": 214.93333330749996, "width": 144.3571428571429, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "\" Caracuta, plow lode,\" No-", "bbox": {"x": 228.2857141046053, "y": 211.5749999845341, "width": 275.2857142857143, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "minale MS.", "bbox": {"x": 93.99999990844157, "y": 238.44166662850375, "width": 107.42857142857143, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "It seems to be the same as", "bbox": {"x": 228.28571402747252, "y": 235.08333331395832, "width": 275.2857142857143, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Plough-land, q. V.", "bbox": {"x": 96.79804916187832, "y": 255.5155659031833, "width": 165.48358917236328, "height": 27.791050978501556}}, {"kind": "list", "text": "A pump; a draw-well. Cornw. A hard blow, Far. dial. Directly; exactly.", "bbox": {"x": 516.4334111680326, "y": 276.0556814153294, "width": 323.02011489868164, "height": 73.39932320117957}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLOWMELL.", "bbox": {"x": 73.52768257555411, "y": 278.23630131826985, "width": 131.34418024335588, "height": 22.473508377869983}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A small wooden hammer occa-", "bbox": {"x": 218.21428543452373, "y": 278.7416666456772, "width": 282, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "sionally fixed to the plough, still used in the North; in the Midland counties in its stead is used a plough-hatchet.", "bbox": {"x": 93.9999998430225, "y": 302.2499999853416, "width": 409.5714285714286, "height": 63.80833333333329}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Weeping.", "bbox": {"x": 207.2896656362292, "y": 364.833750701011, "width": 89.01992348262239, "height": 25.428702775637355}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLOWRING., ploughshare. Kennett.", "bbox": {"x": 71.13153940375747, "y": 354.4537934273065, "width": 360.21144975934715, "height": 77.84018174012505}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Prompt. Paro.", "bbox": {"x": 308.85714264596777, "y": 366.0583332954166, "width": 144.35714285714286, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLOWSHO.", "bbox": {"x": 73.85714246547619, "y": 386.2083329975, "width": 117.5, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLOY.", "bbox": {"x": 70.49999981239496, "y": 409.7166666074019, "width": 70.50000000000001, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A merry-meeting.", "bbox": {"x": 147.71428552434207, "y": 409.71666663573455, "width": 171.21428571428572, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "North.", "bbox": {"x": 332.3571426787946, "y": 409.7166666141927, "width": 63.7857142857143, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLOYE.", "bbox": {"x": 70.49999981615646, "y": 433.2249999600197, "width": 83.92857142857142, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUCK. (1) Courage.", "bbox": {"x": 70.49999975241069, "y": 453.3749999706145, "width": 204.78571428571425, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A plough. Nominale MSỊiẠạo pluck", "bbox": {"x": 169.6739716058292, "y": 412.93671686091807, "width": 336.32643563406805, "height": 65.9616168181102}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Var. dial.", "bbox": {"x": 285.3571426892857, "y": 453.3749999664167, "width": 97.35714285714286, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "up one's heart,\" to be bold, to rejoice. Against the pluck, i. e. against the inclination.", "bbox": {"x": 90.64285628066592, "y": 473.5249998763363, "width": 412.92857142857144, "height": 47.01666666666686}}, {"kind": "list", "text": "To pluck a crow or goose with any one, i. e. to quarrel with him. To pluck a rose, i. e. to go to the jakes, said of women. Middleton, iv. 222. A dry pluck, i. e. a severe stroke. This same is kind cuckolds luck:", "bbox": {"x": 69.26038383123893, "y": 511.6268970955423, "width": 435.00830677577426, "height": 136.578881820043}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "These fellowes have given ine a drie pluck, Now I have never a crose to blesse me.", "bbox": {"x": 107.42857151563528, "y": 648.1583333065535, "width": 349.1428571428571, "height": 40.30000000000003}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Mariageof Witt and Wisdome, 1579.", "bbox": {"x": 218.21428554847563, "y": 688.4583333230945, "width": 278.6428571428572, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(5)", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285695634922, "y": 711.9666665360647, "width": 33.57142857142857, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Our kynge and Robyn rode togyder,", "bbox": {"x": 127.57142839743034, "y": 732.1166666543801, "width": 285.35714285714283, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Forsoth as I you say, And they shote plucke buffet,", "bbox": {"x": 127.57142919249995, "y": 748.9083332661667, "width": 231.64285714285717, "height": 40.299999999999855}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "As they went by the way. Robin Hood, i. 75.", "bbox": {"x": 144.35714279419642, "y": 789.2083333175912, "width": 355.85714285714283, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(6) Same as (1) ?", "bbox": {"x": 66.79117558106569, "y": 809.7079980803137, "width": 165.18521090916224, "height": 28.745083204905097}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "- I had the luck", "bbox": {"x": 238.35714270367353, "y": 836.2249999760119, "width": 127.57142857142857, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "To see, and drink a little pluck.", "bbox": {"x": 167.85714268474905, "y": 856.374999986385, "width": 255.1428571428571, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Brome's Songs, 1661, p. 167.", "bbox": {"x": 285.35714268653396, "y": 876.5249999834836, "width": 214.85714285714283, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(7) A student who fails in an university examination is said to be plucked.", "bbox": {"x": 70.49999970625005, "y": 896.6749998455542, "width": 426.3571428571428, "height": 43.658333333333175}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUCKING.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285697006301, "y": 943.691666641973, "width": 124.21428571428571, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The worsted plucked from the", "bbox": {"x": 204.54600107126217, "y": 938.4170382233592, "width": 295.91872678484236, "height": 27.94043553670257}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "machine while the wheel is turning. North.", "bbox": {"x": 87.28571416821428, "y": 963.8416666536065, "width": 399.5, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUERE.", "bbox": {"x": 66.91542669798946, "y": 983.0103492917542, "width": 97.8120035443987, "height": 25.470967948436737}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUF.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285695634922, "y": 1007.4999999440278, "width": 67.14285714285714, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Weeping. (4.-N.)", "bbox": {"x": 174.5714283998413, "y": 983.9916666405463, "width": 181.28571428571433, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A tube of tin through which boys blow", "bbox": {"x": 134.13778432522196, "y": 1003.8143623777204, "width": 362.89904403686523, "height": 27.959663283824884}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "peas. Linc.", "bbox": {"x": 86.90827771725644, "y": 1027.5752297219713, "width": 111.38663291931152, "height": 22.70385060707722}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Also called a pluffer.", "bbox": {"x": 214.4765227090573, "y": 1024.7792545007953, "width": 192.23886925833568, "height": 28.38969576358795}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUFE.", "bbox": {"x": 67.06235541821967, "y": 1050.8450917155342, "width": 77.37528882707869, "height": 20.776483142375874}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A plough.", "bbox": {"x": 161.14285696101192, "y": 1051.1583332843577, "width": 100.71428571428575, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Yorksh.", "bbox": {"x": 268.50777377678145, "y": 1050.8735658232765, "width": 73.98445211138043, "height": 17.361201600233727}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUFFY. Spongy; porous. Deron. It is sometimes explained, soft, plump.", "bbox": {"x": 70.30837057184945, "y": 1069.2153624096127, "width": 423.51448767525807, "height": 47.56059396266937}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUG.", "bbox": {"x": 67.0715659382738, "y": 1114.7385012540392, "width": 63.92829527173724, "height": 20.606330311298443}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A dwarfish fellow. East.", "bbox": {"x": 150.81576586562983, "y": 1114.1298759941687, "width": 225.42128808157784, "height": 24.213523409763877}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUM. (1) Light; soft.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285696958528, "y": 1138.47499998375, "width": 221.5714285714286, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "West.", "bbox": {"x": 288.71428555761906, "y": 1138.4749999328333, "width": 67.14285714285717, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "list", "text": "Sensible; honest. North. Very; exceedingly.", "bbox": {"x": 66.81655437751755, "y": 1156.1386455283453, "width": 269.0842129843576, "height": 50.43224606513984}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(4) Straight; upright; perpendicular.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285698464697, "y": 1202.283333319823, "width": 355.8571428571429, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Plum", "bbox": {"x": 442.88096736627756, "y": 1201.5623134557334, "width": 54.23806449345184, "height": 21.59203939835221}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "downe, Cotgrave in v. Escarpé.", "bbox": {"x": 90.64285702621065, "y": 1225.7916666467445, "width": 278.6428571428571, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "5) Plum round, quite round.", "bbox": {"x": 73.8571426871875, "y": 1249.299999989505, "width": 271.9285714285714, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "\" Make their", "bbox": {"x": 365.9285712415307, "y": 1245.9416666378809, "width": 130.92857142857136, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "attire to sit plum roundạ Harrison, p. 172", "bbox": {"x": 93.999999906746, "y": 1269.4499999875618, "width": 392.7857142857143, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Plum fat, Florio, p. 33.", "bbox": {"x": 90.64285696921185, "y": 1289.599999979734, "width": 208.14285714285714, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUMAKIN.", "bbox": {"x": 70.50000092321426, "y": 1309.749999748125, "width": 127.57142857142856, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The magnum-bonum plum.", "bbox": {"x": 204.45951778937365, "y": 1310.2213201834331, "width": 249.0487382071359, "height": 24.177047218879018}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUME.", "bbox": {"x": 66.98585906010202, "y": 1332.7183469728418, "width": 90.95685291290285, "height": 27.946639275550915}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "To pick or pluck the feathers off a", "bbox": {"x": 164.4999998266693, "y": 1333.2583333223822, "width": 332.3571428571429, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "hawk or other bird.", "bbox": {"x": 83.92857126071426, "y": 1356.7666666511186, "width": 181.28571428571428, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUMED-SWAN.", "bbox": {"x": 67.1428569649286, "y": 1376.9166666465167, "width": 177.92857142857144, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A white colour. One of the", "bbox": {"x": 241.71428554399589, "y": 1376.9166666520653, "width": 255.1428571428571, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "terms of ancient alchemy.", "bbox": {"x": 87.0674525998085, "y": 1394.0412804989728, "width": 235.5348499843052, "height": 26.918096526463813}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUMMY.", "bbox": {"x": 67.11288978572686, "y": 1420.413842075654, "width": 107.48850577218191, "height": 20.47231578032166}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Soft; wet; mouldy. Devon.", "bbox": {"x": 187.99999980925327, "y": 1420.5749999821908, "width": 258.49999999999994, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUMP. (1) Dry; hard.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285697245676, "y": 1440.7249999821906, "width": 224.92857142857142, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Kent.", "bbox": {"x": 305.49999983214286, "y": 1440.724999921639, "width": 57.07142857142858, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "list", "text": "A clump of trees. North. A crowd of people; a mass of anything.", "bbox": {"x": 67.14285700977041, "y": 1464.2333333174029, "width": 392.7857142857143, "height": 43.65833333333336}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "It", "bbox": {"x": 473.3571426892857, "y": 1484.3833331318335, "width": 23.49999999999997, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "is sometimes a verb,", "bbox": {"x": 87.28571411496306, "y": 1507.891666649296, "width": 204.7857142857143, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "to colleot together.", "bbox": {"x": 295.428571243586, "y": 1507.8916666426787, "width": 201.4285714285714, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "633", "bbox": {"x": 490.14285696101194, "y": 70.5249999160416, "width": 43.64285714285714, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "POC", "bbox": {"x": 708.3571426892858, "y": 70.52499992803567, "width": 53.714285714285666, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "\"Assemble theymselfes in plumpes,\" More's Supplycacyon of Soulys, sig. F. ii.", "bbox": {"x": 537.1428569393939, "y": 107.4666666526266, "width": 416.28571428571433, "height": 47.0166666666665}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Rydes into rowte his dede to revenge, Presede into the plumpe and with a prynce metes,", "bbox": {"x": 536.853364816616, "y": 152.378671073947, "width": 379.9945727757045, "height": 45.904523972670106}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Morte Arthure, MS. Lincoln, f.76.", "bbox": {"x": 678.142856961012, "y": 194.78333331934022, "width": 268.57142857142856, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "When kynge Richard perceved that the people by", "bbox": {"x": 560.4223120268813, "y": 214.63991460660975, "width": 386.4865891592842, "height": 26.768543823560066}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "plumpes fled from hym to Duke Henry.", "bbox": {"x": 537.1428568033278, "y": 235.0833333104357, "width": 318.92857142857144, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Hall's Union, 1548.", "bbox": {"x": 795.6428569710035, "y": 255.2333333053472, "width": 151.07142857142853, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Var. dial. Forby has", "bbox": {"x": 738.5714283883118, "y": 322.39999997862884, "width": 208.14285714285705, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "plumpendicular, perpendicular.", "bbox": {"x": 533.7857140885487, "y": 342.54999998134264, "width": 282, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUM-PORRIDGE.", "bbox": {"x": 516.9999998228174, "y": 362.699999978233, "width": 191.35714285714286, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Porridge with plums in", "bbox": {"x": 721.7857141125284, "y": 366.05833331734124, "width": 224.92857142857136, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "it, a favourite dish at Christmas in some parts of the country.", "bbox": {"x": 536.1850867989607, "y": 378.8621473597578, "width": 410.9916804177421, "height": 57.76534722646076}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "It is mentioned as part of", "bbox": {"x": 705.0000036369047, "y": 406.3583329415279, "width": 245.0714285714286, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Christmas fare in the Humourist, ed. 1724,", "bbox": {"x": 537.1428569630103, "y": 429.86666665467266, "width": 409.5714285714286, "height": 26.86666666666675}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "p. 22, and by Addison.", "bbox": {"x": 536.7780197214049, "y": 446.7861259161342, "width": 198.68485913957866, "height": 27.04857361316681}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUMP-PATE.", "bbox": {"x": 516.9999985564286, "y": 470.16666646516677, "width": 144.3571428571428, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUMPY.", "bbox": {"x": 513.6428569563492, "y": 493.67499996890433, "width": 107.42857142857133, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A thiek-headed fellow.", "bbox": {"x": 674.7857140948179, "y": 473.52499998024507, "width": 214.8571428571429, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "To churn. Corne.", "bbox": {"x": 627.7857121875, "y": 493.674999748125, "width": 181.28571428571428, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUMTEN.", "bbox": {"x": 513.6428569697545, "y": 513.8249999685156, "width": 117.49999999999991, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Plunged. Weber.", "bbox": {"x": 647.9285710608843, "y": 513.8249999440279, "width": 161.14285714285722, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUM-TREE.", "bbox": {"x": 513.6428569661653, "y": 537.3333333068202, "width": 141.00000000000006, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The female pudendum.", "bbox": {"x": 661.3571426662465, "y": 537.3333333069934, "width": 214.85714285714278, "height": 26.86666666666657}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Have", "bbox": {"x": 889.64285668125, "y": 537.3333330814584, "width": 57.07142857142853, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "at the plum tree seems to have been either the burden of a song or a proverbial phrase.", "bbox": {"x": 536.8220798983236, "y": 557.9565593857991, "width": 410.03404998779297, "height": 50.01802078882847}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "It", "bbox": {"x": 919.8571427132654, "y": 584.3499998800597, "width": 26.857142857142776, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "occurs in Middleton, although Mr. Dyce does not seem to be acquainted with the meaning of the term itself, which may be gathered from Cotgrave, in v. Hoche-prunier, and the Mariage of Witt and Wisdome, p. 16.", "bbox": {"x": 533.2332167446042, "y": 602.3925314718435, "width": 414.0532240186419, "height": 111.6817052682241}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUNGE. (1) A deep pool. Somerset", "bbox": {"x": 516.5191467945904, "y": 706.373120477937, "width": 353.40877369471957, "height": 33.40240162611008}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(2) A strait or difficulty. Greene.", "bbox": {"x": 516.9999996957589, "y": 732.1166666421789, "width": 305.5, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUNGY.", "bbox": {"x": 513.642856962088, "y": 752.2666666279167, "width": 100.71428571428572, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Wet; rainy. (4.-N.)", "bbox": {"x": 624.4285712607144, "y": 755.6249999829236, "width": 198.07142857142858, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUNKET. A coarse woollen cloth PLUNKY.", "bbox": {"x": 509.9238101762668, "y": 774.296691769659, "width": 336.3433017730714, "height": 47.88912949562062}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Short; thick; heavy East.", "bbox": {"x": 630.7415902931647, "y": 796.4578625839525, "width": 249.05867603846954, "height": 24.348900713523324}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUNT. A walking-stick, generally one which has a large knob.", "bbox": {"x": 513.2826875075905, "y": 818.2180353903502, "width": 430.2651950291224, "height": 47.05266244411465}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Glouc.", "bbox": {"x": 704.1087232998063, "y": 840.9504423527774, "width": 62.52307183401922, "height": 22.809919488429987}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLURISY.", "bbox": {"x": 513.6428569630102, "y": 863.0916666306845, "width": 100.71428571428572, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Superabundance.", "bbox": {"x": 630.5181908111689, "y": 862.5540541375294, "width": 158.91290255955286, "height": 28.37128311793014}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Shak.", "bbox": {"x": 797.7036759086317, "y": 861.4956268866724, "width": 56.63932500566748, "height": 26.733665808041877}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLUSHES. The thin hoops which hold a besom together.", "bbox": {"x": 513.6428568997537, "y": 883.2416666416595, "width": 429.71428571428567, "height": 43.65833333333336}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "West.", "bbox": {"x": 631.1428567511905, "y": 906.7499998320832, "width": 53.714285714285666, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLY.", "bbox": {"x": 513.6428569362638, "y": 930.2583332687498, "width": 53.714285714285666, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "To bend; to consent, or comply. Still", "bbox": {"x": 574.0714284051401, "y": 930.2583333223482, "width": 369.2857142857143, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "in use in Dorset, Barnes's Gl.", "bbox": {"x": 530.4285713379286, "y": 950.4083333098248, "width": 271.9285714285714, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLYER.", "bbox": {"x": 510.23932578019605, "y": 970.3789589023424, "width": 77.30706228528697, "height": 20.508748733997272}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A very common bawd.", "bbox": {"x": 607.6428569722024, "y": 973.9166666470765, "width": 204.7857142857142, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PLYMOUTH-CLOAK.", "bbox": {"x": 510.285721696099, "y": 990.7083329415278, "width": 208.1428443363734, "height": 23.50833333333325}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A cane, or stick.", "bbox": {"x": 728.4999998144737, "y": 994.0666666401535, "width": 167.85714285714283, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "So", "bbox": {"x": 913.1428569540179, "y": 997.424999895052, "width": 30.214285714285747, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "called, says Ray, ạẠạbecause we use a staff in cuerpo, but not when we wear a cloak.\"", "bbox": {"x": 530.3072426283052, "y": 1015.0867768664649, "width": 413.30280249459395, "height": 46.97459365924205}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "PO.", "bbox": {"x": 510.28571405491067, "y": 1057.8749998740625, "width": 43.64285714285719, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A peacock.", "bbox": {"x": 550.5714284215561, "y": 1061.233333297351, "width": 117.50000000000001, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "（4.-S.）", "bbox": {"x": 681.4999998321429, "y": 1061.2333332803069, "width": 70.49999999999997, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A pruest proud ase a po, Seththe weddeth us bo.", "bbox": {"x": 607.64285686949, "y": 1084.7416666443532, "width": 198.07142857142858, "height": 36.94166666666671}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Wright's Political Songs, p. 159.", "bbox": {"x": 694.674514546801, "y": 1121.486552604158, "width": 245.5715473720006, "height": 24.44503544569001}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "POACHED. Land is said to be poached when it is trodden with holes by heavy cattle. Var.dia.", "bbox": {"x": 509.86943791345107, "y": 1141.6119980285355, "width": 433.69940730503623, "height": 49.97692942619324}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "POACHING.", "bbox": {"x": 510.26079269545403, "y": 1188.7175099438957, "width": 124.26412854875834, "height": 23.77331337134041}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Swampy", "bbox": {"x": 641.2142855069328, "y": 1192.2083332740688, "width": 90.64285714285714, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Devon.", "bbox": {"x": 748.6428565133929, "y": 1188.8499997481251, "width": 70.49999999999997, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "POAD-MILK. The first milk given by cow: after calving.", "bbox": {"x": 512.5869641154331, "y": 1203.9757989176858, "width": 424.4574802943639, "height": 57.13821072181057}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Sussex.", "bbox": {"x": 668.0714284119642, "y": 1235.8666666246875, "width": 77.2142857142857, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "POARE-BLIND.", "bbox": {"x": 510.2857141140422, "y": 1252.6583333104356, "width": 157.78571428571425, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Dim-sighted.", "bbox": {"x": 694.8146255672148, "y": 1255.3984482058536, "width": 124.44217709132604, "height": 24.744770193099903}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The word", "bbox": {"x": 835.9285712607143, "y": 1256.0166666351824, "width": 107.42857142857144, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "occurs in Hollyband's Dictionarie, 1593.", "bbox": {"x": 530.4285713046768, "y": 1276.1666666546728, "width": 369.2857142857143, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "РОЛТ.", "bbox": {"x": 510.2857140981092, "y": 1296.316666607402, "width": 63.78571428571425, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "To kick.", "bbox": {"x": 594.2142854302199, "y": 1296.3166665891665, "width": 80.57142857142856, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Devon.", "bbox": {"x": 684.8571421857143, "y": 1296.3166664147916, "width": 73.85714285714283, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "POBS.", "bbox": {"x": 510.19350420527013, "y": 1319.4287413411032, "width": 70.68441976819719, "height": 17.58418389558803}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Porridge.", "bbox": {"x": 584.1014471510717, "y": 1319.6228315673661, "width": 97.43996238708489, "height": 20.554336766401867}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Craven.", "bbox": {"x": 691.571428039881, "y": 1319.8249998600695, "width": 77.2142857142857, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "POCHE.", "bbox": {"x": 510.2130116868001, "y": 1339.6675313525498, "width": 84.07397624424526, "height": 20.76493720610935}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A pocket.", "bbox": {"x": 607.6231082028335, "y": 1339.882396768804, "width": 94.03949519566129, "height": 20.33520738681156}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "（4.-N.）", "bbox": {"x": 718.4285713026785, "y": 1339.9749999265364, "width": 73.85714285714283, "height": 23.50833333333343}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Unto another she dyde as moche ;", "bbox": {"x": 570.7142855352381, "y": 1363.483333322139, "width": 268.57142857142856, "height": 16.791666666666607}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "For they love none but for theyr poche.", "bbox": {"x": 567.3571426874613, "y": 1383.6333333242073, "width": 312.2142857142857, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The Complaynte of them that ben to late Maryed.", "bbox": {"x": 567.3571426645489, "y": 1400.4249999893948, "width": 372.6428571428571, "height": 20.15000000000011}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "POCHEE.", "bbox": {"x": 510.2857141054233, "y": 1420.5749999626853, "width": 97.35714285714286, "height": 20.149999999999928}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A dish in ancient cookery consisting", "bbox": {"x": 620.8836907296802, "y": 1417.2175124344863, "width": 322.6967767987932, "height": 27.054043920834882}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "principally of poached eggs. Pegge.", "bbox": {"x": 530.3166819830991, "y": 1440.8008638267943, "width": 336.00768225533625, "height": 23.805156775315698}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Potters?", "bbox": {"x": 627.7857141178572, "y": 1464.2333332983505, "width": 87.28571428571428, "height": 16.791666666666785}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "POCHIN.", "bbox": {"x": 510.2213391262963, "y": 1484.089458787776, "width": 90.77160712650847, "height": 20.737749008337634}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "POCHERS. A hedgehog. Somerset.", "bbox": {"x": 511.2843698641816, "y": 1453.3837694661893, "width": 322.69874899727955, "height": 70.65868304570515}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "POCHIT. A pollard tree. Line.", "bbox": {"x": 510.0407526842433, "y": 1504.3616916191202, "width": 299.24198368617465, "height": 26.477575019995385}}], "ms": 335.43175}